{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAw4KXTAEZ1KgWUCQKFY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] With a fixture `node_modules` in a temp directory and a hand-built metafile, notices collect unscoped, scoped, and nested `node_modules` packages and deduplicate by `name@version`.\n[x] Inputs with `bytesInOutput: 0` and inputs outside `node_modules` are ignored.\n[x] A package with no license file, no `license` field, or a license outside the allowlist makes `readBundledPackages` throw an error naming that package.\n[x] Two renders of the same packages are equal, and packages appear sorted by name then version.\n[x] `scripts/check-package.ts` run in a fixture package (copying the real `files` and `license`, with stub files) exits 0 when every required file is present.\n[x] It exits 1 when the tarball lacks `dist/cli.js`, `roast.schema.json`, one of Roast's license files, or `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` (one case each).\n[x] It exits 1 when the manifest declares no `license`, a non-empty `dependencies`, or `optionalDependencies`.\n[x] It exits 1 when `dist/cli.js` has no shebang or is not executable.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` pass; `go test ./...` still passes.\n\nI finished nine of the ten acceptance items. The real-bundle notices item is still open because `@substrate-system/debug` fails the license allowlist, and only you can decide how to fix that.\n\n**Blocker.** `@substrate-system/debug@0.9.68` declares `\"license\": \"SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE\"`, and that file is the Big Time Public License 2.0.2 (free only for noncommercial use and small businesses). Neither is on the allowlist. I added a throwaway `src/debug.ts` that imported it, and `npm run bundle` exited 1 naming that package. I then removed the import, so `debug` is not in the bundle, as the ticket says. The rest of that item passes: every package listed in `dist/meta.json` has a header line in `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`. Your options are to relicense the library, extend the allowlist, or replace it with a small `DEBUG=roast:*` logger in `src/`. I wrote this up in the ticket file. Its one dependency, `supports-color`, is MIT and passes.\n\n**One change from the spec.** `emoji-regex@10.6.0`, which yargs pulls in, ships its license only as `LICENSE-MIT.txt`. The spec's file-name pattern `(\\..*)?` doesn't match that, so the real bundle failed. I widened it to `([.-].*)?`. The check on the `license` field itself is unchanged. This is also recorded on the ticket.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **License library:** `scripts/licenses.ts` collects and checks the bundled packages and renders the notices file. Versions sort numerically, so 2.0.0 comes before 10.0.0.\n- **Bundle step:** `scripts/bundle.ts` now writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`, currently 14 packages, all from the yargs dependency tree.\n- **Package check:** `scripts/check-package.ts` is new and isn't wired into CI or any npm script, as the ticket asks. It accepts an empty `dependencies: {}`, since the spec only rules out a non-empty one, and it fails if `optionalDependencies` is present at all.\n- **Tests:** `test/tooling/licenses.ts` and `test/tooling/check-package.ts`.\n- **Docs:** `AGENTS.md` now covers the license step and the package check.\n\n`npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` (122 assertions) and the full `npm test` (Go plus launcher tests) all pass. Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1575,"cache_read_input_tokens":103120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1575},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c58d9c3b-30b3-4134-a232-a64a183be8